<!-- ══════════════════ SECTION 1 ══════════════════ -->
<h1 class="first">1. Executive Summary</h1>
<p>
  <strong>AccBots</strong> is an enterprise-grade web application created to digitize and scale accounting, bookkeeping, UAE FTA tax advisory, corporate auditing, and business registration services. In addition to a high-converting public marketing front-end, the application embeds a full <strong>Client Portal</strong>, an <strong>Administrative Control Suite</strong>, and two sophisticated financial micro-applications: an <strong>Expense Tracker</strong> with cloud receipt attachment and a <strong>Double-Entry Accounting General Ledger (Accounts-Web)</strong> with dynamic Trial Balance and Profit &amp; Loss reporting.
</p>
<p>
  The platform is designed with an uncompromising standard for <strong>vendor independence</strong>, <strong>data integrity</strong>, and <strong>bank-level web security</strong>. Proprietary third-party authentication widgets have been substituted with a custom stateless JSON Web Token (JWT) architecture backed by relational PostgreSQL persistence and SHA-256 session token hashing.
</p>

<!-- ══════════════════ SECTION 2 ══════════════════ -->
<h1>2. Technology Stack &amp; Language Distribution</h1>
<p>
  The software architecture leverages modern web technologies selected for strict type safety, fast edge execution, and operational cost-efficiency.
</p>

<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>Layer</th>
      <th>Technology / Tool</th>
      <th>Primary Language</th>
      <th>Technical Role &amp; Justification</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Frontend Framework</strong></td>
      <td>Next.js 16 (App Router)</td>
      <td>TypeScript (.tsx)</td>
      <td>Utilizes React Server Components (RSC) for instantaneous initial page loads, edge rendering, SEO optimization, and streaming UI.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Client Engine</strong></td>
      <td>React 19</td>
      <td>TypeScript / JSX</td>
      <td>Provides declarative component management, modern hooks, and seamless hydration across interactive portals.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Styling &amp; Theme</strong></td>
      <td>Tailwind CSS v4 &amp; Base UI</td>
      <td>CSS3 &amp; Utility Classes</td>
      <td>Modern CSS styling incorporating luxury gold accents (<span class="highlight">#C5A85C</span>) and dark/light mode toggle with zero runtime style overhead.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Motion Design</strong></td>
      <td>Framer Motion</td>
      <td>TypeScript</td>
      <td>Smooth client-side micro-animations, accordion reveals, modal transitions, and responsive gestures.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Backend Logic</strong></td>
      <td>Next.js Server Actions</td>
      <td>TypeScript (.ts)</td>
      <td>Direct server-side execution (<span class="highlight">"use server"</span>), eliminating boilerplate REST controllers and providing end-to-end type safety.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Database Engine</strong></td>
      <td>PostgreSQL 15+</td>
      <td>SQL</td>
      <td>Enterprise relational storage with Row-Level Security (RLS) policies, foreign key integrity, check constraints, and analytical SQL views.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Database Client</strong></td>
      <td>postgres.js</td>
      <td>TypeScript</td>
      <td>High-speed, memory-efficient PostgreSQL driver featuring native parameterized tagged template queries to eliminate SQL injection attacks.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Authentication</strong></td>
      <td>jose + bcryptjs</td>
      <td>TypeScript</td>
      <td>Stateless HS256 JWT signing, verification, SHA-256 token hashing, and 12-round bcrypt password hashing.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Data Validation</strong></td>
      <td>Zod 4</td>
      <td>TypeScript</td>
      <td>Strict schema validation enforcing field types, length constraints, and format checks across all forms and Server Actions.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Object Storage</strong></td>
      <td>Cloudflare R2 (via AWS S3 SDK)</td>
      <td>TypeScript</td>
      <td>S3-compatible zero-egress cloud storage for company assets, team portraits, blog banners, and expense invoice receipts.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Email Delivery</strong></td>
      <td>Resend</td>
      <td>TypeScript / HTML</td>
      <td>Transactional email infrastructure delivering branded client welcome emails, password reset links, and real-time contact notifications.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Hosting &amp; CI/CD</strong></td>
      <td>Railway (PaaS)</td>
      <td>Nixpacks / Docker</td>
      <td>Automated deployment directly from GitHub commits, serving Next.js via optimized standalone container output.</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<!-- ══════════════════ SECTION 3 ══════════════════ -->
<h1>3. Database Architecture &amp; Connectivity</h1>

<h2>3.1 Connection Strategy &amp; Resilience</h2>
<p>
  The database is hosted on Supabase's managed PostgreSQL infrastructure located in the <span class="highlight">aws-0-ap-southeast-1</span> region. Connection management is governed through the <strong>PgBouncer Transaction Pooler</strong> on port <span class="highlight">6543</span>.
</p>

<div class="card-box">
  <div class="card-box-title">Critical Architectural Solution: URL Dotted Username Handling</div>
  <p>
    Supabase transaction pooler URLs format the username as <span class="highlight">postgres.[project-ref]</span>. Default URL parsers erroneously interpret the dot as a hostname separator, resulting in runtime <span class="highlight">ENOTFOUND tenant/user</span> errors. In <span class="highlight">src/lib/db.ts</span>, discrete URL parameters are parsed programmatically and supplied directly into the connection pool.
  </p>
</div>

<h2>3.2 Atomic Financial Transactions</h2>
<p>
  For complex operations in the Accounts-Web general ledger, multi-split journal entries require absolute ACID compliance. AccBots employs atomic transaction boundaries (<span class="highlight">sql.begin(async (tx) =&gt; { ... })</span>) to ensure that if a credit or debit entry fails, all corresponding insertions are rolled back immediately, preserving mathematical integrity.
</p>

<h2>3.3 Complete Schema &amp; Table Reference</h2>
<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>Table Name</th>
      <th>Primary Purpose</th>
      <th>Key Columns &amp; Constraints</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>users</strong></td>
      <td>Central user account store</td>
      <td>id (UUID PK), full_name, email (UNIQUE), password_hash, role ('super_admin','admin','user'), is_active</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>refresh_tokens</strong></td>
      <td>Session persistence &amp; revocation</td>
      <td>id (UUID PK), user_id (FK users), token_hash (UNIQUE SHA-256), expires_at, revoked_at</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>password_reset_tokens</strong></td>
      <td>Cryptographic password recovery</td>
      <td>id (UUID PK), user_id (FK users), token_hash (UNIQUE), expires_at, used_at</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>contact_messages</strong></td>
      <td>Lead capture from public forms</td>
      <td>id (UUID PK), name, email, phone, subject, message, is_read (BOOL), created_at</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>services</strong></td>
      <td>Advisory service packages</td>
      <td>id (UUID PK), title, slug (UNIQUE), icon, short_description, benefits (ARRAY), process_steps (JSONB), faqs (JSONB)</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>website_settings</strong></td>
      <td>Dynamic site configuration</td>
      <td>id (UUID PK), key (UNIQUE), value, category ('general','contact','seo','social'), updated_at</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>testimonials</strong></td>
      <td>Client ratings &amp; reviews</td>
      <td>id (UUID PK), name, company, role, content, avatar_url, rating (1-5)</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>team_members</strong></td>
      <td>Executive leadership bios</td>
      <td>id (UUID PK), name, role, bio, avatar_url, linkedin_url, sort_order</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>blog_posts</strong></td>
      <td>CMS knowledge base articles</td>
      <td>id (UUID PK), title, slug (UNIQUE), excerpt, content, cover_image, author_id (FK users), is_published</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>activity_logs</strong></td>
      <td>Security and audit tracking</td>
      <td>id (UUID PK), user_id (FK users), action, entity_type, entity_id, metadata (JSONB), ip_address</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>expense_categories</strong></td>
      <td>Budget classification</td>
      <td>id (UUID PK), name (UNIQUE), description, budget_limit, is_active</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>expenses</strong></td>
      <td>Corporate expense filings</td>
      <td>id (UUID PK), user_id (FK users), category_id (FK), amount, currency, receipt_url, status ('pending','approved','rejected')</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>accounts</strong></td>
      <td>General Ledger Chart of Accounts</td>
      <td>id (UUID PK), code (UNIQUE), name, type ('asset','liability','equity','revenue','expense'), is_active</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>transactions</strong></td>
      <td>Journal voucher headers</td>
      <td>id (UUID PK), reference_number (UNIQUE), description, transaction_date, created_by (FK users)</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>journal_entries</strong></td>
      <td>Double-entry debit/credit splits</td>
      <td>id (UUID PK), transaction_id (FK CASCADE), account_id (FK RESTRICT), debit, credit, description (CHECK: balanced splits)</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>trial_balance (View)</strong></td>
      <td>Dynamic accounting trial balance</td>
      <td>account_id, code, name, type, total_debit, total_credit, net_balance (Calculated real-time via SQL aggregation)</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<!-- ══════════════════ SECTION 4 ══════════════════ -->
<h1>4. Security Architecture &amp; Perimeter Defense</h1>
<ul>
  <li><strong>HTTP Hardening:</strong> Configured in <span class="highlight">next.config.ts</span> with <span class="highlight">nosniff</span>, <span class="highlight">X-Frame-Options: DENY</span>, <span class="highlight">Referrer-Policy</span>, and <span class="highlight">Permissions-Policy</span>.</li>
  <li><strong>Custom JWT Authentication:</strong> HS256 signed access tokens (15 min expiry) combined with database-tracked SHA-256 hashed refresh tokens (7-30 days).</li>
  <li><strong>Cookie Defense:</strong> Set with <span class="highlight">HttpOnly</span>, <span class="highlight">Secure</span>, and <span class="highlight">SameSite=Lax</span> to insulate against XSS and CSRF token extraction.</li>
  <li><strong>Edge Proxy Route Guard:</strong> Located in <span class="highlight">src/proxy.ts</span>, validating permissions and triggering automatic token refresh in the background.</li>
  <li><strong>Role-Based Access Control:</strong> Strict boundary enforcement for <span class="highlight">super_admin</span>, <span class="highlight">admin</span>, and <span class="highlight">user</span>.</li>
</ul>

<!-- ══════════════════ SECTION 5 ══════════════════ -->
<h1>5. Hosting &amp; Infrastructure Details</h1>
<ul>
  <li><strong>PaaS Host:</strong> Railway using custom Nixpacks deployment running Next.js standalone container.</li>
  <li><strong>Database Host:</strong> Supabase PostgreSQL (AWS ap-southeast-1) with transaction pooling on port 6543.</li>
  <li><strong>Storage CDN:</strong> Cloudflare R2 bucket (<span class="highlight">accbot-main-website</span>) with public edge distribution and signed uploads.</li>
  <li><strong>Email Infrastructure:</strong> Resend API sending transactional emails with custom domain verification.</li>
</ul>

